================================================================================
PART 2: UNDERSTANDING BOOTSTRAP ICONS
================================================================================

WHAT ARE BOOTSTRAP ICONS?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bootstrap Icons is an open-source icon library.

It can be used through several approaches:

• Icon font

• Inline SVG

• SVG sprite

• Individual SVG files


For this lesson, we use the:

ICON FONT + CSS CLASS

approach.


Example:

<i
  className="bi bi-trash"
  aria-hidden="true"
></i>


================================================================================
IMPORTANT: BOOTSTRAP ICONS != BOOTSTRAP CSS
================================================================================

You do NOT need to install the complete Bootstrap CSS framework merely to use
Bootstrap Icons.

Bootstrap Icons can be used independently.


For this lesson:

React
   +
Our Custom CSS
   +
Bootstrap Icons


We are NOT automatically adding:

Bootstrap Grid

Bootstrap Buttons

Bootstrap Forms

Bootstrap JavaScript


================================================================================
ICON CLASS PATTERN
================================================================================

Bootstrap Icons normally use:

bi
+
bi-ICON-NAME


Example:

bi bi-trash


Another:

bi bi-pencil-square


Another:

bi bi-plus-circle


Conceptually:

bi
 ↓
Base Bootstrap Icon class


bi-trash
 ↓
Specific glyph


