ICON-ONLY CONTROL
       ↓
CONTROL NEEDS ACCESSIBLE NAME


================================================================================
PART 5: STYLING BOOTSTRAP ICONS
================================================================================

Bootstrap icon-font icons inherit:

currentColor


and commonly size with:

font-size


This makes them easy to style with normal CSS.


================================================================================
GroceryItem.css - ICON STYLES
================================================================================

.item-meta i,
.item-unit-price i {

  margin-right:
    6px;
}


.item-meta i {

  color:
    #667eea;

  font-size:
    1rem;
}


.item-unit-price i {

  color:
    #666;

  font-size:
    0.9rem;
}


.btn-action i {

  font-size:
    1.15rem;

  line-height:
    1;
}


.btn-edit i {

  color:
    currentColor;
}


.btn-delete i {

  color:
    currentColor;
}


/* Hover */

.btn-action:hover i {

  transform:
    scale(1.1);
}


/* Icon Transition */

.btn-action i {

  transition:
    transform 0.2s ease;
}


/* Purchased */

.item-card.purchased
.item-meta i {

  color:
    #666;
}


================================================================================
WHY currentColor?
================================================================================

Suppose:

.btn-delete {

  color:
    #b71c1c;
}


The icon can inherit:

currentColor


This avoids repeating the same color declaration for:

button
+
icon


Conceptually:

BUTTON COLOR
     ↓
currentColor
     ↓
ICON


================================================================================
ICON SIZE
================================================================================

Bootstrap icon-font icons can be sized using:

font-size


Example:

.bi {

  font-size:
    1rem;
}


Large action icon:

.btn-action i {

  font-size:
    1.2rem;
}


================================================================================
RESPONSIVE SIZING
================================================================================

Usually icons do NOT need dramatically different sizes at every breakpoint.

Example:

@media (
  max-width: 480px
) {

  .btn-action i {

    font-size:
      1.05rem;
  }

}


The important requirement is that the complete interactive control remains
large enough and easy to use.

Don't shrink a button merely because the viewport is smaller.


================================================================================
ICON STYLING TABLE
================================================================================

+---------------------------+------------------------------------------+
| SELECTOR                  | PURPOSE                                  |
+---------------------------+------------------------------------------+
| .item-meta i              | Metadata icons                           |
| .item-unit-price i        | Unit-price icon                          |
| .btn-action i             | Action icons                             |
| .btn-action:hover i       | Hover feedback                           |
| .item-card.purchased i    | Purchased visual state                   |
+---------------------------+------------------------------------------+


