PART 8: ICON ACCESSIBILITY
================================================================================

ACCESSIBILITY RULE 1:
DECORATIVE ICON + VISIBLE TEXT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:

<button type="submit">

  <i
    className="bi bi-plus-circle"
    aria-hidden="true"
  ></i>

  Add Item

</button>


The visible text already describes the control.

Therefore:

aria-hidden="true"


on the decorative icon is appropriate.


================================================================================
ACCESSIBILITY RULE 2:
ICON-ONLY BUTTON
================================================================================

Example:

<button
  type="button"
  aria-label="Delete Milk"
>

  <i
    className="bi bi-trash"
    aria-hidden="true"
  ></i>

</button>


The BUTTON needs the accessible name.


================================================================================
ACCESSIBILITY RULE 3:
DECORATIVE METADATA ICON
================================================================================

Example:

<span>

  <i
    className="bi bi-tag"
    aria-hidden="true"
  ></i>

  Dairy

</span>


The visible word:

Dairy


already supplies meaning.


================================================================================
ACCESSIBILITY RULE 4:
DO NOT RELY ON title ALONE
================================================================================

title="Delete item"


can provide a pointer tooltip in some environments.

But it should not replace a proper accessible name.


Use:

aria-label="Delete Milk"


for an icon-only button.


================================================================================
ACCESSIBILITY RULE 5:
KEEP THE INTERACTIVE ELEMENT SEMANTIC
================================================================================

GOOD:

<button>
  icon
</button>


NOT:

<i
  onClick={...}
></i>


Why?


button provides built-in:

• Keyboard semantics

• Focus behavior

• Activation behavior

• Button role


================================================================================
DO YOU NEED sr-only?
================================================================================

Not always.


If using:

<button
  aria-label="Delete Milk"
>

  <i
    aria-hidden="true"
  ></i>

</button>


the accessible name already comes from:

aria-label


Adding another screen-reader-only:

Delete


can become redundant.


Use one clear accessible naming strategy.


================================================================================
ACCESSIBILITY PATTERN TABLE
================================================================================

+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| SITUATION               | PATTERN                                    |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| Icon + Visible Text     | aria-hidden on icon                        |
| Icon-only Button        | aria-label on button                       |
| Decorative Icon         | aria-hidden="true"                         |
| Meaningful Standalone   | Provide accessible name                    |
| Interactive Action      | Use button/link semantics                  |
| Keyboard User           | Visible :focus-visible style               |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
PART 9: ICON ANIMATIONS AND EFFECTS
================================================================================

Animations are optional.

Use them only when they communicate something useful.


================================================================================
SPIN - LOADING
================================================================================

<i
  className="
    bi
    bi-arrow-repeat
    icon-spin
  "
  aria-hidden="true"
></i>


CSS:

@keyframes iconSpin {

  to {

    transform:
      rotate(360deg);
  }

}


.icon-spin {

  animation:
    iconSpin
    1s
    linear
    infinite;
}


Potential use:

Loading / processing indicator


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A spinning decorative icon alone should NOT be the only indication that
something is loading.

Use accompanying status text/state.


================================================================================
PULSE - ATTENTION
================================================================================

@keyframes iconPulse {

  0%,
  100% {

    opacity:
      1;
  }


  50% {

    opacity:
      0.55;
  }

}


.icon-pulse {

  animation:
    iconPulse
    2s
    ease-in-out
    infinite;
}


Use sparingly.

Continuous movement can become distracting.


================================================================================
FADE IN - STATUS CHANGE
================================================================================

@keyframes iconFadeIn {

  from {

    opacity:
      0;
  }


  to {

    opacity:
      1;
  }

}


.icon-fade-in {

  animation:
    iconFadeIn
    0.3s
    ease;
}


This can be appropriate for:

• Success confirmation

• Newly displayed status


================================================================================
HOVER SCALE
================================================================================

.btn-action i {

  transition:
    transform 0.2s ease;
}


.btn-action:hover i {

  transform:
    scale(1.1);
}


This gives subtle feedback without continuous animation.


================================================================================
REDUCED MOTION
================================================================================

Always consider:

prefers-reduced-motion


Example:

@media (
  prefers-reduced-motion:
  reduce
) {

  .icon-spin,
  .icon-pulse,
  .icon-fade-in {

    animation:
      none;
  }


  .btn-action i {

    transition:
      none;
  }


  .btn-action:hover i {

    transform:
      none;
  }

}


================================================================================
ANIMATION TABLE
================================================================================

+----------------------+---------------------------+
| EFFECT               | POTENTIAL USE             |
+----------------------+---------------------------+
